window.docContents[91].resolve({"/Constructions/#section-kneser-graphs":{"contents":"The k-th Kneser graph M. Kneser, Aufgabe 360 [Problem 360], Jahresber. Deutsch. Math.-Verein. 58 (1955), no. 2, 27. See also Martin Kneser, Collected Works, Springer, 2021, 729–742. on a type β has as vertices the\nk-element subsets of β, with edges between any distinct disjoint subsets. Before\nwe can define this as a SimpleGraph we need to decide what the vertex type should\nbe. If we are happy to work with finite types (i.e. to assume Fintype β) then we\ncould use (Finset.univ : Finset β).powersetCard k which is the finite family of\nk-element subsets of a finite type β.\n\n#check Finset.powersetCard\n\n\nUsing Finset.powersetCard gives us easy access to lots of counting results about\nfamilies of finite sets, which would be useful.\n\nBut there are two drawbacks. Firstly, the finiteness assumption is a bit restrictive.\nSecondly, this vertex type mentions Finset.univ, and hence the Fintype β\ninstance: two different instances give vertex types that are equal but not\ndefinitionally equal, so a lemma proved for one does not apply to the other. (Since\nwe won't use this definition we mark it private.)\n\n@[simps]\nprivate def kneserGraphFintype (β : Type*) [Fintype β] (k : ℕ) :\n    SimpleGraph ((Finset.univ : Finset β).powersetCard k) where\n  Adj u v := Disjoint u.val v.val ∧ u ≠ v\n  symm := ⟨fun _ _ h => ⟨h.1.symm, h.2.symm⟩⟩\n  loopless := ⟨fun _ h => h.2 rfl⟩\n\n\nInstead we use the subtype of Finset β consisting of k-element subsets, i.e.\n{s : Finset β // s.card = k}. This means we no longer need to assume Fintype β\nbut we lose direct access to the Finset.powersetCard results. However we can solve\nthis issue with a simple translation lemma saying that, for any predicate p,\ncounting the k-element subsets satisfying p as terms of the subtype\n{s : Finset β // s.card = k} gives the same answer as counting them as members of\nthe family (Finset.univ : Finset β).powersetCard k. (See\nIndependence Number of the Kneser Graph for details.)\n\nThe k-th Kneser graph on β: vertices are k-element subsets of β, and\nedges join disjoint, distinct subsets./-- The k-th Kneser graph on β: vertices are k-element subsets of β, and\nedges join disjoint, distinct subsets. -/\n@[simps]\ndef kneserGraph (β : Type*) (k : ℕ) :\n    SimpleGraph {s : Finset β // s.card = k} where\n  Adj u v := Disjoint u.val v.val ∧ u ≠ v\n  symm := ⟨fun _ _ h => ⟨h.1.symm, h.2.symm⟩⟩\n  loopless := ⟨fun _ h => h.2 rfl⟩\n\n\n#check kneserGraph_adj -- (kneserGraph β k).Adj u v = (Disjoint ↑u ↑v ∧ u ≠ v)\n\n\ninstance (β : Type*) (k : ℕ) [DecidableEq β] :\n    DecidableRel (kneserGraph β k).Adj := fun u v => by\n  unfold kneserGraph; infer_instance\n\n\nWe introduce the notation Kn[n, k] for the k-th Kneser graph on Fin n.\n\nKn[n, k] is the Kneser graph kneserGraph (Fin n) k: its vertices are the\nk-element subsets of Fin n, and edges join disjoint, distinct subsets./-- Kn[n, k] is the Kneser graph kneserGraph (Fin n) k: its vertices are the\nk-element subsets of Fin n, and edges join disjoint, distinct subsets. -/\nscoped notation \"Kn[\" n \", \" k \"]\" => kneserGraph (Fin n) k\n\n\nA special case of the Kneser graph is the Petersen graph J. Petersen, Sur le théorème de Tait [On Tait's theorem], L'Intermédiaire des Mathématiciens 5 (1898), 225–227.,\nwhich is Kn[5, 2].\n\nThe Petersen graph which is the Kneser graph Kn[5, 2]./-- The *Petersen* graph which is the Kneser graph Kn[5, 2]. -/\nabbrev petersenGraph : SimpleGraph {s : Finset (Fin 5) // s.card = 2} := Kn[5, 2]\n\n\nThe Petersen graph as the Kneser graph Kn(5,2)\n\nWe will look at the independence number of Kn[n, k] in Cliques\nand colourings of Kn[n, k] in Exercises Colorings. Computing its\nindependence number is really just a case of translating the Erdős–Ko–Rado theorem\n(which is in Mathlib) into the language of SimpleGraph.\n\nend SimpleGraph\n\n\nnamespace SimpleGraph\n\n\n","context":"Graph Theory in Lean\u0009Constructions","header":"3.7. Kneser Graphs*","id":"/Constructions/#section-kneser-graphs"}});